---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Wörgl: money with a shelf life, a hackathon project on NEAR testnet" description="Wörgl coins lose 1% on a fixed schedule, and what melts goes into a pot the community spends again. A hackathon project, live on NEAR testnet." active="/">

<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <h1 id="hero-title">Money with a shelf life.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Spend it, or it flows back to the town.</p>
  <p class="prose">Wörgl is a token on NEAR. Its coins lose 1% on a fixed schedule, and what melts goes into a pot the community spends again.</p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a class="button solid" href="/try">Try it free</a>
    <a class="button" href="/idea">How it works</a>
  </div>
  <p class="hero-note">Free. Runs on NEAR testnet. No wallet needed.</p>

  <div class="window" aria-label="Live Wörgl note">
    <div class="window-bar">
      <span><i class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i>Live on NEAR testnet</span>
      <span>Demo speed: 1% per <span data-period>hour</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="window-body">
      <div class="window-note">
        <svg id="note" viewBox="0 0 960 420" role="img" aria-label="A sample Wörgl note. Its value counts down in real time, and a bar shows how much has melted into the town pot. Drag it sideways to move through time."></svg>
        <p class="note-caption">A sample note that started at 100 coins when you opened the page. Drag it sideways, or use the controls, to jump ahead.</p>
        <div class="note-controls">
          <div class="group" id="note-rate" role="group" aria-label="Melt speed">
            <div class="seg">
              <button type="button" data-rate="demo" aria-pressed="true">Demo speed</button>
              <button type="button" data-rate="real" aria-pressed="false">Real speed</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="group"><span class="label">Skip ahead</span><span id="note-presets" class="chips"></span></div>
          <div>
            <label for="note-slider" class="sr-only">Move the note through time</label>
            <input id="note-slider" type="range" min="0" max="1000" step="1" value="0">
          </div>
          <p id="note-readout" class="readout"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="window-panel">
        <p id="data-status" class="status" role="status"></p>
        <div class="panel-stats">
          <div class="stat"><p class="label">In the town pot</p><p class="figure-cell treasury" id="v-treasury">–</p></div>
          <div class="stat"><p class="label">In people's hands</p><p class="figure-cell" id="v-circ">–</p></div>
          <div class="stat"><p class="label">Can be paid out today</p><p class="figure-cell treasury" id="v-allow">–</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="panel-check">
          <p class="label">Checked in your browser</p>
          <p class="panel-check-line" id="verify-summary">Running the checks…</p>
          <a href="#check-title">See what is checked</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="rates-title">
  <h2 id="rates-title">Two speeds</h2>
  <p class="prose">The demo is fast so you can watch it happen. A real DAO would use the slow setting.</p>
  <div class="notes-pair">
    <div class="mini-note">
      <h3>This demo</h3>
      <p class="mini-big">1% every <span data-period>hour</span></p>
      <p>100 coins become <b class="num" data-demo-day>78.57</b> after a day, and <b class="num" data-demo-week>18.48</b> after a week.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mini-note">
      <h3>Real setting</h3>
      <p class="mini-big">1% every month</p>
      <p>100 coins become <b class="num" data-real-month>99.00</b> after a month, and <b class="num" data-real-year>88.49</b> after a year.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
  <div class="loop-row">
    <figure class="figure">
      <svg id="loop" viewBox="0 0 480 430" role="img" aria-label="A loop. The town pot pays people through payouts. People trade with each other. Everything melts back to the town pot."></svg>
    </figure>
    <ol class="plain-steps big">
      <li><b>The town pot pays people.</b> A group vote, called a DAO, approves the payouts.</li>
      <li><b>People spend and trade.</b> Holding costs a little, so coins are made to be used.</li>
      <li><b>Everything melts back.</b> Each balance loses 1% on a schedule, and the loss returns to the pot.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <p class="callout">The DAO decides who gets paid. The contract decides how much can be paid.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="use-title">
  <h2 id="use-title">What it is for</h2>
  <p class="prose">Coins that expire suit money that is meant to be used. Both examples use the real setting, 1% a month.</p>
  <div class="uses">
    <div class="use">
      <h3>Grants that come back if unspent</h3>
      <p>A fund sends a team 5,000 coins. If they sit untouched for three months, <b class="num" data-grant-left>4,851.50</b> are left and <b class="num" data-grant-back>148.50</b> are back in the pot for the next grant.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="use">
      <h3>Community and event credits</h3>
      <p>Hand out 20 credits for a street festival. A month later <b class="num" data-credit-month>19.80</b> are left, and after six months <b class="num" data-credit-six>18.83</b>, so they are worth using soon.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="check-title">
  <h2 id="check-title">Check it yourself</h2>
  <p class="prose">Everything on this page is read from the contract on NEAR. Your browser recomputes the key numbers with its own copy of the maths.</p>
  <ul class="verify" id="verify-out" aria-live="polite"><li><span class="pass">…</span><span>Reading the contract</span></li></ul>
  <div class="row">
    <button id="verify-run" type="button">Run the checks again</button>
    <a href="/maths">How the maths works</a>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">Contract <a id="home-token" href="#"></a>, run by the DAO <a id="home-dao" href="#"></a>. The code is on <a id="home-repo" href="#">GitHub</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="section end-cta" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
  <h2 id="cta-title">Try it in 60 seconds</h2>
  <p class="prose">Claim some test coins, send a few to a friend, and watch the pot grow. No wallet needed.</p>
  <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button solid" href="/try">Try it free</a><a class="button" href="/faq">Read the FAQ</a></div>
</section>
</Base>
